    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@62767",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "WARWICK.\nFather, the Duke hath told the truth;\nThus got the house of Lancaster the crown.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@62767/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 8,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@62767/line-2",
          "start": 9,
          "end": 46,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@62767/line-3",
          "start": 47,
          "end": 89,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 2325581,
        "end": 2325705,
        "line": 85201,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap13/p@62767",
        "anchor": "sceneII_13.2"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "WARWICK.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@62895",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "YORK.\nWhich now they hold by force and not by right;\nFor Richard, the first son’s heir, being dead,\nThe issue of the next son should have reigned.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@62895/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 5,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@62895/line-2",
          "start": 6,
          "end": 52,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@62895/line-3",
          "start": 53,
          "end": 99,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@62895/line-4",
          "start": 100,
          "end": 146,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 2325709,
        "end": 2325895,
        "line": 85207,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap13/p@62895",
        "anchor": "sceneII_13.2"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "YORK.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@63085",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "SALISBURY.\nBut William of Hatfield died without an heir.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@63085/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 10,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@63085/line-2",
          "start": 11,
          "end": 56,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 2325899,
        "end": 2325985,
        "line": 85214,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap13/p@63085",
        "anchor": "sceneII_13.2"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "SALISBURY.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 10
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@63175",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "YORK.\nThe third son, Duke of Clarence, from whose line\nI claim the crown, had issue, Philippa, a daughter,\nWho married Edmund Mortimer, Earl of March.\nEdmund had issue, Roger, Earl of March;\nRoger had issue, Edmund, Anne, and Eleanor.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@63175/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 5,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@63175/line-2",
          "start": 6,
          "end": 54,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@63175/line-3",
          "start": 55,
          "end": 106,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@63175/line-4",
          "start": 107,
          "end": 150,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@63175/line-5",
          "start": 151,
          "end": 190,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@63175/line-6",
          "start": 191,
          "end": 234,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 2325989,
        "end": 2326273,
        "line": 85219,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap13/p@63175",
        "anchor": "sceneII_13.2"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "YORK.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@63463",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "SALISBURY.\nThis Edmund, in the reign of Bolingbroke,\nAs I have read, laid claim unto the crown\nAnd, but for Owen Glendower, had been king,\nWho kept him in captivity till he died.\nBut to the rest.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@63463/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 10,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@63463/line-2",
          "start": 11,
          "end": 52,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@63463/line-3",
          "start": 53,
          "end": 94,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@63463/line-4",
          "start": 95,
          "end": 138,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@63463/line-5",
          "start": 139,
          "end": 178,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@63463/line-6",
          "start": 179,
          "end": 195,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 2326277,
        "end": 2326522,
        "line": 85228,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap13/p@63463",
        "anchor": "sceneII_13.2"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "SALISBURY.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 10
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-second-part-of-king-henry-the-sixth/sceneII_13.2/p@63712",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "YORK.\nHis eldest sister, Anne,\nMy mother, being heir unto the crown,\nMarried Richard Earl of Cambridge, who was son\nTo Edmund Langley, Edward the Third’s fifth son.\nBy her I claim the kingdom; she was heir\nTo Roger, Earl of March, who was the son\nOf Edmund Mortimer, who married Philippa,\nSole daughter unto Lionel, Duke of Clarence.\nSo, if the issue of the elder son\nSucceed before the younger, I am king.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
